WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
Hey there, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, episode 65 for June 8th, 2026.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.920
Let's break down today's coolest AI news, so anyone can understand it.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:10.520
Let's go.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.820
So imagine you have a sketchbook that only gives you one page at a time before it slams

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.080
shut.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.520
That is exactly how free chat GPT accounts used to feel when you tried to make pictures.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.940
The good news is that limit just caught much bigger for many users.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:32.980
People are now reporting they can create 10 or even 15 images back to back before any slowdown shows up.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.740
The same change applies to uploading files for the AI to read and understand.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.180
Think of it like suddenly getting a full pack of colored pencils instead of just one stub.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.180
The old rules made the free version feel like a quick demo you could only peek at.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:53.800
The new ones turn it into a real creative workspace you can visit again and again during the day.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:59.600
This matters because making images is one of the most fun ways beginners first meet AI.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.500
You can turn a history report into illustrated scenes or design posters for a school event.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:12.680
For students and hobbyists it closes the gap between wishing you could see an idea and actually watching it appear on screen.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.300
The update is rolling out gradually so some accounts still have the old limits while others already enjoy the jump.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.020
If your account has not changed yet just keep checking back over the next few days.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.520
To try it right now open chat GPT on your phone or laptop and make sure you are on a free account.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.340
Type a prompt like draw a friendly robot helping with homework in a cartoon style.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:40.500
Keep going with new prompts and see how many you can make before any waiting message appears.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.340
Okay now for my favorite part of the show where we look under the hood.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:49.640
You know how when you are texting a friend your phone guesses the next word before you finish typing.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.280
Now picture that same auto complete working on pictures instead of words.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.460
The AI has studied millions of photos to learn what usually comes next in a scene.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.340
First it breaks your text prompt into small pieces it understands.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.120
Then it starts with random noise like static on an old TV.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:13.800
It slowly removes the noise piece by piece while checking against everything it learned about shapes, colors and objects.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:20.160
Each step is basically asking given this prompt what should this tiny part of the picture look like.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.340
After many quick passes the static turns into a clear image that matches your description.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.140
And that is basically what image generating AI is doing when it creates pictures from your words.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:38.720
So next time someone says diffusion model you can tell them it is basically super powered auto complete for pictures.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:44.140
Not so scary right? Now let us look at some other cool stuff worth trying.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.900
Open AI is reportedly planning a big refresh for chat GPT in the next few weeks.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:58.220
The new version is expected to feel smarter and more helpful for everyday tasks like writing, answering questions and brainstorming.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:06.880
This matters because chat GPT is still the AI most beginners meet first so changes here reach millions of students and curious users.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:13.240
When the update arrives try asking it to explain a topic from your homework in three different styles.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:19.780
Ask for one like a friend texting one like a teacher and one like a YouTuber to see what feels most useful.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:27.360
Next up Kpop fans are pushing back against realistic fake videos and images made without the artist's permission.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:33.820
These deep fakes can look convincing but often twists someone's likeness into uncomfortable situations.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:41.920
The story shows why learning to spot AI generated media is becoming an everyday skill especially on social platforms.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:50.420
You can practice by searching for AI deep fake examples on a trusted site and comparing them side by side with real photos to train your eye.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.520
Here are a couple of quick bits to wrap up the news.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:04:04.200
One AI researcher suggests saving your hardest or most unusual ideas for work or hobbies because AI is making it cheaper to turn good ideas into finished projects.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.960
The bottleneck is shifting from how do I build this to what should I build.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:11.700
AI agents are moving fast too.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.440
Just a year ago the most advanced AI helpers could only answer questions.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:25.760
Today they can take actions across multiple tools which is exciting but also means we need to think carefully about safety as they get more powerful.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:27.480
And that is a wrap.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:32.360
If any of today's stories made you go, huh that is cool go play with it.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.160
Curiosity is how every expert started.

